#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063937 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064347 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97dc4044-9984-58a3-bf02-61f31fc31792" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "46597138-36cc-584b-ade8-70cbfafcad2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12905" :question/problem "Solve the equation $4x = y$ for the variable $x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $x.$ To do this, we treat $y$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nIn this case, we simply divide both sides of the equation by $4\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\t4x &= y \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {4x} {4} &= \\dfrac y 4 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {{\\cancel{4}}x} {\\cancel{4}} &= \\dfrac y 4 \\[5pt]\n\t\tx &= \\dfrac y4\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063938 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74cfd55f-4e24-5f97-ba42-28fa410866a7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Multi-Step Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "3237ac51-d473-548d-b316-9425717c22bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12907" :question/problem "Solve the following equation for the variable $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x-2y}{3}=\\dfrac{1+2y}{4}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $x.$ First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-2y}{3} & =\\frac{1+2y}{4} \\\\ 4\\cdot (3x-2y) & =3\\cdot (1+2y) \\\\ 12x-8y & =3+6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $8y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-8y & =3+6y \\\\ 12x-8y+8y & =3+6y+8y \\\\ 12x & =3+14y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $12\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x & =3+14y \\\\ \\frac{12x}{12} & =\\frac{3+14y}{12} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{12}x}{\\cancel{12}} & =\\frac{3+14y}{12} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3+14y}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063950 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064348 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "075c23a4-9de9-59b5-bec4-575b0b0454f4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "84e24683-73f6-59a1-b2c3-03d3659adf27" :question/math-academy-id "e-13119" :question/problem "Given that $\\dfrac{x}{3} + 2y = 1,$ express $x$ in terms of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $x.$ To do this, we treat $y$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we subtract $2y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3}+2y & =1 \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}+2y-2y & =1-2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}+0 & =1-2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{3} & =1-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3} & =1-2y \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{x}{3} & =3\\cdot (1-2y) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\cancel{3}} & =3\\cdot (1-2y) \\\\ x & =3\\cdot (1-2y) \\\\ x & =3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2y \\\\ x & =3-6y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064348 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "075c23a4-9de9-59b5-bec4-575b0b0454f4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09fc2719-481a-56be-83d9-d2f80fde45e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487583} {:answer/id #uuid "4923f559-c0e3-50d9-a454-99a67e6b45d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487709} {:answer/id #uuid "5af203fd-56ef-5bec-8966-1f9e7b63b08e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487751} {:answer/id #uuid "6f01e7f1-4738-56d5-b28e-ede5ffadc778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487787} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24c2b-71c1-564b-befe-52b1f3fee82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5af203fd-56ef-5bec-8966-1f9e7b63b08e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487751} :answer-field/id #uuid "85896fbd-038e-5e22-b120-6db4ab42220d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2257e81b-6df1-53bd-bf2f-94399c3d9e90" :question/math-academy-id "q-135010" :question/problem "If $\\frac{x}{2}-5y=2y$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $x.$ To do this, we treat $y$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we add $5y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-5y & =2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}-5y+5y & =2y+5y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =2y+5y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =7y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =7y \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} & =2\\cdot 7y \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\cancel{2}} & =2\\cdot 7y \\\\ x & =2\\cdot 7y \\\\ x & =14y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064347 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97dc4044-9984-58a3-bf02-61f31fc31792" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0af86761-a9fa-5095-b46e-f4192d60519c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487587} {:answer/id #uuid "961ed85d-7443-58b0-880a-f94e2896754b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487849} {:answer/id #uuid "adf07b29-c7b3-52bc-9a49-baeac9d1d4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{v}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487898} {:answer/id #uuid "b1cab5ab-fbec-575c-bd0f-8a8613314644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{v}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487904} {:answer/id #uuid "ec287634-588f-5b16-b335-d55640aec956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{v}{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1cab5ab-fbec-575c-bd0f-8a8613314644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{v}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487904} :answer-field/id #uuid "18653a7d-dd36-525c-82ee-2649adb843b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f182666-9412-501e-b641-7f7f9b2222ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-135478" :question/problem "If $u+\\frac{v}{2}=1,$ then $u=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $u.$ To do this, we treat $v$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nIn this case, we simply subtract $\\frac{v}{2}$ from both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+\\frac{v}{2} & =1 \\\\ u+\\frac{v}{2}-\\frac{v}{2} & =1-\\frac{v}{2} \\\\ u+0 & =1-\\frac{v}{2} \\\\ u & =1-\\frac{v}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74cfd55f-4e24-5f97-ba42-28fa410866a7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Multi-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "541438b0-3d68-5da1-8797-bf586ce1dc59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3y-2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "541438b0-3d68-5da1-8797-bf586ce1dc59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3y-2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487734} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3558bc4-d6aa-5a60-9e85-1a7a6d4326f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a062c0fa-ba5c-540d-bad1-e5dc2b1fdc72" :question/math-academy-id "q-176623" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{2x+1}{3}=\\frac{y-x}{2},$ express $x$ in terms of $y.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $x.$ First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{3} & =\\frac{y-x}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot (2x+1) & =3\\cdot (y-x) \\\\ 4x+2 & =3y-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we subtract $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & =3y-3x \\\\ 4x+2-2 & =3y-3x-2 \\\\ 4x & =3y-3x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $3x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =3y-3x-2 \\\\ 4x+3x & =3y-3x-2+3x \\\\ 7x & =3y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x & =3y-2 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =\\frac{3y-2}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}x}{\\cancel{7}} & =\\frac{3y-2}{7} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3y-2}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064347 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97dc4044-9984-58a3-bf02-61f31fc31792" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56fc4b27-f7c3-5872-8859-927fb33cd902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56fc4b27-f7c3-5872-8859-927fb33cd902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487739} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4d897ea-bb5f-5d9d-a846-ffc2b250e5d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b63796bb-cd51-5db1-b65b-8d15ce564d53" :question/math-academy-id "q-178560" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{h}{8}=k,$ express $h$ in terms of $k.$\n\n$h=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $h.$ To do this, we treat $k$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nIn this case, we simply multiply both sides of the equation by $8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{8} & =k \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{h}{8} & =8\\cdot k \\\\ \\cancel{8}\\cdot \\frac{h}{\\cancel{8}} & =8k \\\\ h & =8k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74cfd55f-4e24-5f97-ba42-28fa410866a7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Multi-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a84c382-4383-56de-89ba-57cf705ab259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7-4x}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a84c382-4383-56de-89ba-57cf705ab259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7-4x}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487586} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb6684c5-888a-5cbe-9a9a-85f61f6107dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a390d02a-3ecf-5fc0-8eb1-0f04dc4eff6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-178606" :question/problem "Given that $4x-y=7-5y,$ express $y$ in terms of $x.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $y.$ To do this, we treat $x$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we add $5y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =7-5y \\\\ 4x-y+5y & =7-5y+5y \\\\ 4x+4y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $4x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4y & =7 \\\\ 4x+4y-4x & =7-4x \\\\ 4y & =7-4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y & =7-4x \\\\ \\frac{4y}{4} & =\\frac{7-4x}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}y}{\\cancel{4}} & =\\frac{7-4x}{4} \\\\ y & =\\frac{7-4x}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064348 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "075c23a4-9de9-59b5-bec4-575b0b0454f4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26d15348-de8a-535f-9e64-8f40de85b7b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487645} {:answer/id #uuid "369c4ab5-25fe-5787-9d2a-b79cf9f1a13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487671} {:answer/id #uuid "98b0d511-17df-5228-b13c-11db536cb6fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487855} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cacec0-819c-5ea4-bb89-0d22d5e3708d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487952} {:answer/id #uuid "de9e3631-aa7b-50c9-834a-9fdd000bc4f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de9e3631-aa7b-50c9-834a-9fdd000bc4f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487990} :answer-field/id #uuid "e91bb9a3-ffd8-5aa1-b8a8-a7e51a400fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cb21341-1ec0-588f-b6f2-da7ac9131ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-2611" :question/problem "If $6x+3y=3$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $y.$ To do this, we treat $x$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we subtract $6x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+3y & =3 \\\\ 6x+3y-6x & =3-6x \\\\ 6x-6x+3y & =3-6x \\\\ 3y & =3-6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y & =3-6x \\\\ 3y & =3(1-2x) \\\\ \\frac{3y}{3} & =\\frac{3(1-2x)}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}y}{\\cancel{3}} & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}(1-2x)}{\\cancel{3}} \\\\ y & =1-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
